          <avActivityHighlights>New snow and wind slabs at intermediate and high altitudes.</avActivityHighlights>
          <avActivityComment>Over a wide area 30 to 40 cm of snow has fallen since yesterday above approximately 1500 m. &lt;br/&gt; The new snow of yesterday is in some cases prone to triggering. The sometimes moderate wind has transported the new snow. &lt;br/&gt; In particular adjacent to ridgelines and in gullies and bowls small and, in isolated cases, medium-sized avalanches are possible. In addition the soft wind slabs are capable of being triggered. &lt;br/&gt; &lt;br/&gt; The Avalanche Warning Service currently has only a small amount of information that has been collected in the field.</avActivityComment>
